WHEREAS, the purpose and intent of the Town Council of the Town of Clermont is to protect the health, safety, general welfare and property values of the citizens of the Town, through the enactment of a comprehensive set of regulations governing signs in the Town, and by the development of a proposed sign ordinance, to maintain an aesthetically attractive town in which signs are compatible with the surrounding area, to insure the protection of free speech rights under the United States and Georgia Constitutions within the Town, and fo regulate the erection and placement of permanent signs within the Town in order to provide safe operating conditions for pedestrian and vehicular traffic without unnecessary and unsafe distractions to drivers and pedestrians;

WHEREAS, the Town of Clermont, in order to bave a comprehensive plan of regulations regarding signs within the Town, needs a temporary planning period of 190 days in order to develop appropriate regulations within a sign ordinance regarding permanent signs and appropriate zoning provi sions regarding signs; -

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia finds that it is appropriate for the Town of Clermont, Georgia to impose a temporary moratorium on rezonings or the issuance of building permits, or both, regarding permanent signs;

WHEREAS, the Town Council of the Town of Clermont, Georgia finds that it is appropriate to narrowly tailor this temporary moratorium to only apply against permanent signs, but allow all other development as provided and regulated by the current ordinances of the Town.

